text:
alex: Hey team — running into a weird combo with the JS SDK + Expo dev client (Hermes). Metro fails resolving the SDK's ESM entry and then crypto/getRandomValues blows up at runtime. stack trace points to 'global.crypto' undefined and 'ReadableStream' missing. Anyone seen this? :confused:

sam: Ugh yes. ESM exports + RN packager is still touchy. Is the SDK distributed with an exports field that points only to ESM? That can make Metro pick the wrong entry.

alex: Exactly. package.json has "exports": { "./package.json": "./package.json", "./": { "import": "dist/index.mjs", "require": "dist/index.cjs" } } — Metro picks the import entry and then we hit `crypto` imports that expect Node.

marta: Two quick things we've used: 1) provide Metro resolver overrides to prefer cjs, 2) polyfill crypto/getRandomValues and ReadableStream. For Expo dev client (Hermes) we used `react-native-get-random-values` + `expo-random` as fallback.

ben: Paste of the metro patch we added a while ago:```js
// metro.config.js
const path = require('path')
module.exports = {
  resolver: {
    extraNodeModules: {
      crypto: path.resolve(__dirname, 'shims/crypto.js')
    },
    preferNativePlatform: false,
  },
};
```

alex: Nice. My issue is also TypeScript defs — the SDK's types import `stream` types and that causes tsc to pull in Node lib defs, breaking RN projects unless "skipLibCheck" is on. Any ideas to avoid shipping node-specific types?

sam: If upstream can't separate types, we did a tiny d.ts wrapper in our app to remap or declare the missing types: `declare module 'node:stream' { export * from 'stream'; }` — not ideal. Better if SDK ships a `types/react-native.d.ts` and conditional exports for types.

marta: Another runtime workaround for ReadableStream: shim with `web-streams-polyfill` or implement a tiny adapter that converts async iterables to RN-friendly chunks. Example shim:```js
// shims/stream.js
if (!global.ReadableStream) {
  global.ReadableStream = require('web-streams-polyfill/ponyfill').ReadableStream;
}
```

alex: Tried that, but Hermes + Expo's dev client sometimes still complains about Symbol.asyncIterator not existing. Ended up patching SDK import sites that do `for await (const chunk of stream)` to use `stream[Symbol.asyncIterator] ? for await... : fallbacks`. Painful but works.

ben: On the auth/retry front — note that our SDK's automatic token refresh uses a global fetch wrapper that relies on `AbortController`. In RN you need polyfill for AbortController or fetch behavior differs and retries never happen. We added `abortcontroller-polyfill` in our app.

alex: Any thoughts on long-term fixes we could raise in SDK repo issues? I can open a PR proposal but want to list concrete asks.

sam: Request list: 1) publish CJS entry point in `main` for packagers that prefer require (or add `react-native` field in package.json pointing to a RN-specific build). 2) Ship separate types that avoid Node libs (or conditional types). 3) Document RN+Expo compatibility guide (polyfills + metro config). 4) Add opt-in lightweight browser/edge build that excludes Node-only runtime bits.

marta: +1 and add: publish a tiny UMD/browser build with minimal deps for RN dev client and edge runtimes — keeps streams/crypto shims optional.

alex: I'll draft an issue/PR with those bullets. For anyone blocked right now, here's a quick checklist we used to get running locally: 1) npm i react-native-get-random-values web-streams-polyfill abortcontroller-polyfill 2) add shims to top of entry:```js
import 'react-native-get-random-values';
import 'abortcontroller-polyfill/dist/abortcontroller-polyfill-only';
import './shims/stream';
```
3) metro.config.js mapping for crypto -> shims/crypto.js 4) tsconfig: set "skipLibCheck": true until upstream fixes types 5) pin SDK to cjs build with a resolver override or by importing require('sdk/dist/index.cjs')

ben: Saved — also FYI expo-bot: new dev client release notes mention improved compatibility for `global.crypto` in SDKs starting SDK 48. Might reduce some friction.

expo-bot: Heads up — Expo SDK 48+ provides `crypto.getRandomValues` in managed runtimes; native dev clients may still need polyfills for older versions. See https://blog.expo.dev/ (link).

marta: Thanks — that's helpful. Alex, LMK when you open the issue and I can add repro steps and the metro config snippet.

alex: Will do. I'll include a tiny repro app (expo prebuild) and steps to reproduce on Hermes. Thanks all :thumbsup:
